{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FXYwm31LSDNiZHTL1Xhzi6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implement `parse_duration` in `duration.py`\n2\t\n3\tOur job scheduler accepts human-written timeouts. Implement `parse_duration(s: str) -> int`,\n4\treturning a whole number of **seconds**, or raising `ValueError` for anything invalid.\n5\tPython 3.9, standard library only. Follow the grammar exactly; anything not allowed below is invalid.\n6\t\n7\t## Form A: unit form\n8\t- One or more `<number><unit>` parts. Units: `w` (week, 604800 s), `d` (86400), `h` (3600),\n9\t  `m` (60), `s` (1). Lowercase only.\n10\t- `<number>` is digits, optionally with a decimal part: `1`, `10`, `1.5`, `0.25`. No leading `.`\n11\t  (`.5h` is invalid), no trailing `.` (`5.h` is invalid). Leading zeros are fine (`05m`).\n12\t- Units must appear in strictly decreasing size and each at most once (`1h30m` ok, `30m1h` and\n13\t  `1h1h` invalid).\n14\t- Parts may be separated by single spaces or written together (`1h 30m` = `1h30m`). No space\n15\t  between a number and its unit (`1 h` is invalid). No other separators.\n16\t- The total must be a whole number of seconds after exact (not floating point) arithmetic:\n17\t  `1.5m` = 90 is fine, `0.3s` is invalid, `0.1h` = 360 is fine.\n18\t\n19\t## Form B: clock form\n20\t- `H:MM:SS` or `M:SS`. The first field is one or more digits with no upper limit; the other fields\n21\t  are exactly two digits and must be `00`–`59`. No decimals. `1:30` = 90, `1:00:00` = 3600,\n22\t  `90:00` = 5400, `1:60` invalid, `1:5` invalid.\n23\t\n24\t## Both forms\n25\t- Leading and trailing whitespace is ignored. Inner whitespace is only allowed as in Form A.\n26\t- An optional single leading `-` makes the result negative (`-1h` = -3600, `-1:30` = -90).\n27\t  `+` is not allowed. `-0s` = 0.\n28\t- The bare string `0` is valid and means 0. Any other bare number (`5`, `1.5`) is invalid.\n29\t- Empty or whitespace-only input is invalid. Non-`str` input raises `TypeError`.\n30\t\n31\t## Examples\n32\t```\n33\tparse_duration(\"1h30m\")    -> 5400\n34\tparse_duration(\" 2d 4h \")  -> 187200\n35\tparse_duration(\"1.5h\")     -> 5400\n36\tparse_duration(\"1w2d3h4m5s\") -> 788645\n37\tparse_duration(\"1:02:03\")  -> 3723\n38\tparse_duration(\"-45s\")     -> -45\n39\tparse_duration(\"0\")        -> 0\n40\t```\n41\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efabdb89-9c20-443d-9b90-fa55dc1caf38","uuid":"2eb65758-db09-409a-afac-5e85abb665e9","timestamp":"2026-10-31T12:30:03.285Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/<path>","content":"# Implement `parse_duration` in `duration.py`\n\nOur job scheduler accepts human-written timeouts. Implement `parse_duration(s: str) -> int`,\nreturning a whole number of **seconds**, or raising `ValueError` for anything invalid.\nPython 3.9, standard library only. Follow the grammar exactly; anything not allowed below is invalid.\n\n## Form A: unit form\n- One or more `<number><unit>` parts. Units: `w` (week, 604800 s), `d` (86400), `h` (3600),\n  `m` (60), `s` (1). Lowercase only.\n- `<number>` is digits, optionally with a decimal part: `1`, `10`, `1.5`, `0.25`. No leading `.`\n  (`.5h` is invalid), no trailing `.` (`5.h` is invalid). Leading zeros are fine (`05m`).\n- Units must appear in strictly decreasing size and each at most once (`1h30m` ok, `30m1h` and\n  `1h1h` invalid).\n- Parts may be separated by single spaces or written together (`1h 30m` = `1h30m`). No space\n  between a number and its unit (`1 h` is invalid). No other separators.\n- The total must be a whole number of seconds after exact (not floating point) arithmetic:\n  `1.5m` = 90 is fine, `0.3s` is invalid, `0.1h` = 360 is fine.\n\n## Form B: clock form\n- `H:MM:SS` or `M:SS`. The first field is one or more digits with no upper limit; the other fields\n  are exactly two digits and must be `00`–`59`. No decimals. `1:30` = 90, `1:00:00` = 3600,\n  `90:00` = 5400, `1:60` invalid, `1:5` invalid.\n\n## Both forms\n- Leading and trailing whitespace is ignored. Inner whitespace is only allowed as in Form A.\n- An optional single leading `-` makes the result negative (`-1h` = -3600, `-1:30` = -90).\n  `+` is not allowed. `-0s` = 0.\n- The bare string `0` is valid and means 0. Any other bare number (`5`, `1.5`) is invalid.\n- Empty or whitespace-only input is invalid. Non-`str` input raises `TypeError`.\n\n## Examples\n```\nparse_duration(\"1h30m\")    -> 5400\nparse_duration(\" 2d 4h \")  -> 187200\nparse_duration(\"1.5h\")     -> 5400\nparse_duration(\"1w2d3h4m5s\") -> 788645\nparse_duration(\"1:02:03\")  -> 3723\nparse_duration(\"-45s\")     -> -45\nparse_duration(\"0\")        -> 0\n```\n","numLines":41,"startLine":1,"totalLines":41}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FXYwm31LSDNiZHTL1Xhzi6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
